  "description": "The Ursell body-order cumulants of any complete-graph assembly are the finite differences of its coordination weight w(z) = B(A)/C(A,2): b_n = C(n,2) * Delta^{n-2} w(1). A reparameterisation, exact, deriving no magnitude — it turns an infinite tower of many-body coefficients into one function of one integer variable, and gives the pairwise wall (w constant), the Mayer sign (w non-increasing) and the A>=5 blow-up (finite differences of a peaked w) a single common cause.",
